# A leading slash anchors a pattern to this directory; a pattern with no slash
# matches at any depth. Several rules below were anchored by accident and so
# never matched the paths they named — where a rule is deliberately anchored or
# deliberately not, the reason is written next to it.

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
build/
dist/
*.db

# ── Node / Next.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Playwright ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately unanchored. These are written next to whichever config ran, and
# this repo runs suites from both the root and frontend/. The previous
# `frontend/`-anchored rules missed the root copies completely, which is how
# `test-results/.last-run.json` and `artifacts/` ended up in git status — and
# how the former was committed.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
artifacts/
# Anchored on purpose: `tmp/` alone is too generic to ignore repo-wide.
frontend/tmp/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deny every .env variant, then re-admit the committed templates. Listing each
# secret file individually meant a new one — .env.staging, .env.production —
# was tracked by default and stayed that way until someone noticed. This fails
# in the safe direction instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# ── Uploaded documents ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reachable only when STORAGE_BACKEND=local and UPLOAD_DIR points inside the
# repo; the default is object storage. Unanchored, because the previous
# `/tmp/research_factory_uploads/` form was rooted here and so matched
# <repo>/tmp/..., never the system /tmp path it appeared to name.
research_factory_uploads/

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log

# ── OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Editors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .vscode/ was tracked for a while on the theory that it was shared editor
# config. It held one key disabling an AI extension's MCP prompt — a personal
# preference, not a project setting. Nothing here needs a committed editor
# config; add one back only if a setting is required to build or test.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Local AI tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Assistant workspaces and vendored skill packs. Machine-local and not part of
# the project.
.gemini/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
